@startuml
title Smart Product Framework - End-to-End Sequence Flow

actor "Product Provider" as PProvider
actor Client
participant "Frontend / dApp" as Frontend
participant "TextResource\n(terms XML)\n----\nITextResource" as XmlResource
participant "TextResource\n(documentation XSLT)\n----\nITextResource" as XsltResource
participant "ClientRegistry\n\n----\nIClientRegistry" as ClientRegistry
participant "TradableBondDataRegistry\n\n----\nIProductDefinitionRegistry" as Registry
participant "CurveIndications" as CurveRegistry
participant "ProductFactoryRegistry\n(generic)" as Factory
participant "SimpleBondFactory\n(product-specific)" as Deployer
participant "SimpleBond\n(deployed product)" as Bond
participant "EvmXmlRenderer" as Renderer

== Initial Setup ==

PProvider -> ClientRegistry : deploy ClientRegistry(owner)
PProvider -> Registry : deploy TradableBondDataRegistry(owner, clientRegistry)
PProvider -> Factory : deploy ProductFactoryRegistry(owner, registry)
PProvider -> Registry : setProductFactory(factory)
Registry -> Factory : productRegistryAddress()
Factory --> Registry : registry (back-reference check)

== Register a Product Factory (here: SimpleBondFactory) ==

PProvider -> Deployer : deploy SimpleBondFactory(genericFactory)
PProvider -> Factory : registerProductFactory(SIMPLE_BOND_TYPE, deployer)
Factory -> Deployer : supportsInterface(IProductSpecificFactory)
Deployer --> Factory : true
Factory -> Deployer : productTypeId()
Deployer --> Factory : SIMPLE_BOND_TYPE (type match)
Factory -> Factory : store Active factory configuration
Factory --> PProvider : ProductFactoryRegistered

note right of Factory
The generic factory is the source of truth for:
productTypeId -> active product-specific factory.
end note

== Resource Publication ==

PProvider -> XmlResource : deploy TextResource(owner, BOND_TERMS,\n"application/xml", bytes(""), bytes32(0))
loop for every terms chunk
	PProvider -> XmlResource : appendChunk(chunk)
end
PProvider -> XmlResource : finalize(keccak256(content))
XmlResource -> XmlResource : read chunks + verify hash + lock resource
XmlResource --> PProvider : finalized terms resource

PProvider -> XsltResource : deploy TextResource(owner, BOND_STYLESHEET,\n"application/xslt+xml", bytes(""), bytes32(0))
loop for every stylesheet chunk
	PProvider -> XsltResource : appendChunk(chunk)
end
PProvider -> XsltResource : finalize(keccak256(content))
XsltResource -> XsltResource : read chunks + verify hash + lock resource
XsltResource --> PProvider : finalized stylesheet resource

note over XmlResource, XsltResource
TextResource also supports one-shot publication by passing
content and its expected hash to the constructor. Demo04 uses
the staged appendChunk + finalize workflow shown above.
end note

== Product Definition Publication ==

PProvider -> Registry : publishProductDefinition({name, {terms, stylesheet, productTypeId}})

Registry -> XmlResource : supportsInterface(ITextResource)
XmlResource --> Registry : true
Registry -> XmlResource : isFinalized()
XmlResource --> Registry : true
Registry -> XmlResource : resourceType()
XmlResource --> Registry : BOND_TERMS

Registry -> XsltResource : supportsInterface(ITextResource)
XsltResource --> Registry : true
Registry -> XsltResource : isFinalized()
XsltResource --> Registry : true
Registry -> XsltResource : resourceType()
XsltResource --> Registry : BOND_STYLESHEET

Registry -> Registry : productDefinitionId = keccak256(abi.encode(name, address(this)))
Registry -> Registry : store ProductDefinitionStorage\n(status = Active, version = 1)
Registry --> PProvider : ProductDefinitionPublished + StatePartUpdated

PProvider -> Registry : computeProductDefinitionId(name)
Registry --> PProvider : productDefinitionId\n(partId = uint256(productDefinitionId))

note over PProvider, Client
The registry's statePartXmlTemplate(partId) includes the terms
and stylesheet with parse="text". This is a source preview:
evmstate bindings are returned as text and are not evaluated
against the registry.
end note

== Indication Publication and Assignment ==

PProvider -> CurveRegistry : deploy CurveIndications(owner)
PProvider -> CurveRegistry : publishCurveIndications(curveName, quotes[])
CurveRegistry -> CurveRegistry : curveId = keccak256(abi.encode(curveName, address(this)))
CurveRegistry -> CurveRegistry : store active quote board + touch indication version
CurveRegistry --> PProvider : IndicationPublished + StatePartUpdated
PProvider -> PProvider : derive indicationId / curveId

PProvider -> Registry : assignProductIndication(productDefinitionId, curveRegistry, indicationId)
Registry -> CurveRegistry : supportsInterface(IProductIndication)
CurveRegistry --> Registry : true
Registry -> CurveRegistry : indicationStatus(indicationId)
CurveRegistry --> Registry : Active
Registry -> CurveRegistry : indicationCategory()
CurveRegistry --> Registry : CURVE
Registry -> Registry : _isAcceptedIndication(productTypeId, CURVE) == true
Registry -> CurveRegistry : partIdForIndication(indicationId)
CurveRegistry --> Registry : indicationPartId
Registry -> Registry : store (curveRegistry, indicationId, partId)\nand increment product-definition version
Registry --> PProvider : ProductIndicationAssigned + StatePartUpdated

note right of Registry
Registry stores per productDefinitionId:
- terms + stylesheet resources
- productTypeId
- (productIndication, indicationId, partId)

Assignment accepts Active or Suspended indications.
Current trade creation does not re-check indication liveness.
end note

== Client Registration ==

PProvider -> ClientRegistry : registerClient({client, lei})
ClientRegistry -> ClientRegistry : store status = Active
ClientRegistry --> PProvider : ClientRegistered + ClientStatusChanged

== Frontend Prepares Trade Request ==

Client -> Frontend : select product definition

Frontend -> Registry : productIndicationOfDefinition(productDefinitionId)
Registry --> Frontend : indicationContract, indicationId, partId

Frontend -> Renderer : render indication(contract, partId)
Renderer -> CurveRegistry : statePartXmlTemplate(partId)
CurveRegistry --> Renderer : lean XML template with\nevmstate:args="$partId" callbacks
Renderer -> CurveRegistry : indicationStatusByPartId(partId)
CurveRegistry --> Renderer : status
Renderer -> CurveRegistry : activeQuoteCountByPartId(partId)
CurveRegistry --> Renderer : quote count
Renderer -> CurveRegistry : activeQuotesByPartId(partId)
CurveRegistry --> Renderer : QuoteView[]
Renderer -> Renderer : expand quote rows and format fields
Renderer --> Frontend : curve indication XML

Frontend -> Registry : productTypeByDefinitionId(productDefinitionId)
Registry --> Frontend : productTypeId

Frontend -> Factory : productFactoryOf(productTypeId)
Factory --> Frontend : specific factory address

Frontend -> Deployer : productSpecificPayloadSchema()
Deployer --> Frontend : schema string
Frontend -> Deployer : productSpecificSchemaHash()
Deployer --> Frontend : schema hash

note right of Frontend
productSpecificPayloadSchema() is a concrete-factory helper;
it is not currently declared by IProductSpecificFactory.

SimpleBond payload fields:
- notional
- maturity
end note

Frontend -> Frontend : ABI-encode productSpecificPayload
Frontend -> Frontend : attach productSpecificSchemaHash

== Trade Request and Deployment ==

Client -> Frontend : submit trade request
Frontend -> Registry : createTradeRequest({productDefinitionId, schemaHash, payload})\n(client-signed transaction)

Registry -> Registry : require productFactory set
Registry -> Registry : load ProductDefinitionStorage(productDefinitionId)
Registry -> Registry : require product definition Active

Registry -> ClientRegistry : isEligibleClient(client, productDefinitionId)
ClientRegistry --> Registry : true

Registry -> Factory : canDeployProduct(productTypeId)
Factory --> Registry : true

Registry -> Registry : tradeId = keccak256(abi.encode(\nregistry, chainId, nonce, client, productDefinitionId))
Registry -> XmlResource : contentHash()
XmlResource --> Registry : termsContentHash
Registry -> XsltResource : contentHash()
XsltResource --> Registry : stylesheetContentHash
Registry -> Registry : deploymentStateHash = keccak256(abi.encode(\ncommon state, resource addresses + hashes,\nschemaHash, keccak256(payload)))

Registry -> Factory : deployProduct({common, schemaHash, payload})

Factory -> Factory : require msg.sender == productRegistryAddress
Factory -> Factory : load factory configuration for productTypeId
Factory -> Factory : require configuration Active
Factory -> Factory : require tradeId unused

Factory -> Deployer : deployProduct({common, schemaHash, payload})

Deployer -> Deployer : require msg.sender == genericFactory
Deployer -> Deployer : require schemaHash == productSpecificSchemaHash()
Deployer -> Deployer : require common.productTypeId == productTypeId()

Deployer -> Bond : new SimpleBond(common, payload)
Bond -> Bond : store immutable common state
Bond -> Bond : productSpecificFactory = msg.sender (deployer)
Bond -> Bond : status = Requested\n emit TradeStatusChanged(Requested, Requested)
Bond -> Bond : _applyTerms(payload) -> decode + validate
Bond -> Bond : emit StateUpdated
Bond --> Deployer : product address

Deployer -> Deployer : isFactoryDeployedProduct[product] = true
Deployer --> Factory : product

Factory -> Factory : productByTradeId[tradeId] = product
Factory -> Factory : emit ProductDeployed
Factory --> Registry : product

Registry -> Registry : _productByTradeId[tradeId] = product
Registry -> Registry : emit TradeRequestCreated
Registry --> Frontend : transaction event contains tradeId + product
Frontend --> Client : product deployed (status Requested)

== Trade Lifecycle (incept / confirm) ==

opt client amends terms while Requested
	Client -> Frontend : update terms
	Frontend -> Bond : updateTerms(payload)\n(client-signed transaction)
	Bond -> Bond : require client + status Requested
	Bond -> Bond : _applyTerms(payload)
	Bond -> Bond : emit TermsUpdated + StateUpdated
	Bond --> Frontend : ok
end

PProvider -> Frontend : read current terms hash
Frontend -> Bond : currentTermsHash()
Bond --> Frontend : agreedTermsHash

PProvider -> Bond : inceptTrade(agreedTermsHash)
Bond -> Bond : require product provider + status Requested
Bond -> Bond : require agreedTermsHash == currentTermsHash()
Bond -> Bond : store agreedTermsHash\nstatus = Incepted
Bond -> Bond : emit TradeStatusChanged + TradeIncepted
Bond --> PProvider : ok

Client -> Bond : confirmTrade(agreedTermsHash)
Bond -> Bond : require client + status Incepted
Bond -> Bond : require agreedTermsHash == stored hash
Bond -> Bond : status = Active
Bond -> Bond : emit TradeStatusChanged + TradeConfirmed + TradeActivated
Bond -> Bond : _onActivated() (product-specific hook)
Bond --> Client : trade Active

== Product XML Rendering and Presentation ==

Client -> Frontend : open product
Frontend -> Renderer : render(product)

Renderer -> Bond : stateXmlTemplate()
Bond -> XmlResource : contentHash()
XmlResource --> Bond : terms integrity hash
Bond -> XsltResource : contentHash()
XsltResource --> Bond : stylesheet integrity hash
Bond --> Renderer : SimpleBond XML with DeploymentState\nand web3:// XIncludes for terms and stylesheet

Renderer -> XmlResource : text() via terms XInclude
XmlResource --> Renderer : terms XML
Renderer -> XsltResource : text() via stylesheet XInclude
XsltResource --> Renderer : XSLT XML

Renderer -> Renderer : resolve no-argument evmstate:call bindings\nagainst the deployed SimpleBond
Renderer -> Bond : productRegistry(), productSpecificFactory(),\ntradeId(), parties, definition data, tradeStatus(), ...
Bond --> Renderer : deployment and lifecycle values
Renderer -> Bond : notional()
Bond --> Renderer : value
Renderer -> Bond : maturity()
Bond --> Renderer : value

Renderer -> Renderer : identity-transform / serialize resolved XML
Renderer --> Frontend : resolved product XML

Frontend -> XsltResource : text()
XsltResource --> Frontend : stylesheet
Frontend -> Frontend : apply XSLT to resolved XML\n(Demo04 presentation step)
Frontend --> Client : display rendered product document

note right of Renderer
EvmXmlRenderer resolves XIncludes and no-argument
evmstate bindings. During state-part rendering it also
supports one uint256 callback argument supplied as $partId.
It does not currently execute XSLT;
Demo04 applies the stylesheet separately.
end note

@enduml
